     .. versionchanged:: 3.0
         Added the ``default`` parameter.
 
+    Hierarchical grouping can be done by specifying multiple attributes
+    with the ``levels`` parameter. Each attribute defines one level,
+    in order. The attribute can be a list or a comma-separated string.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        <ul>{% for dept, roles in users|groupby(["department", "role"], levels=2) %}
+          <li>{{ dept }}
+            <ul>{% for role, members in roles %}
+              <li>{{ role }}: {{ members|map(attribute="name")|join(", ") }}
+            {% endfor %}</ul>
+          </li>
+        {% endfor %}</ul>
+
+    .. versionchanged:: 3.0
+        Added the ``default`` parameter.
+
     .. versionchanged:: 2.6
